  "name": "Adventure Mode applies its difficulty auras and experience modifiers",
  "contract": "Issue #4978. Each Adventure Mode (211) tier is one main aura plus two difficulty (SLS) auras in Ascension's Spell.dbc: tier 1 is 302053 with 302054 (+49% physical damage taken, -26% PvE damage done) and 302058 (+50% magic damage taken, -15% healing done); tier 100 is 302882 with 302883 and 302884. The difficulty auras follow the main aura on and off. The main aura's XP effects are SPELL_AURA_MOD_XP_PCT with an XP-source mask in the misc value (1 creature kills, 2 quests): tier 1 is +100% with mask 18 and -50% with mask 5, so quests grant twice and creature kills half the experience a character outside the mode receives. The mode's NO_FETCH_QUEST_EXPERIENCE rule reads 'no experience from quests with no objectives': A Threat Within (783, talk to Marshal McBride) awards nothing, while Wolves Across the Border (33, collect items) and Kobold Camp Cleanup (7, kill kobolds) still award experience, as A Threat Within does for a character outside the mode. Experience is read within the current level, and a doubled quest reward nearly fills level 1 (397 of 400), so every character whose experience gain is asserted afterwards earns it without crossing a level: the item-collection quest is rewarded to tier1 before its last kill, and the tapper starts its kill with no experience. The wolves keep their natural 42 health so the player-damage requirement is met and the kill awards full experience. Ratios allow for the integer truncation of the realm XP rates. The tier 1 difficulty aura 302054 also carries SPELL_AURA_MOD_DAMAGE_DONE_VERSUS (341) at -26%, so the same melee swing against the same wolf deals 74% of what a character outside the mode deals. Tier 1 monsters have 100% more health: the first hit from a tier 1 player doubles an untapped creature's maximum health. COSMETIC_ELITE_ENEMIES shows hostile creatures as elite: while tier1 is in the mode the creature query response for the hostile wolf (299) carries rank 1 and the friendly Marshal McBride (197) keeps rank 0; leaving the mode resends the wolf's normal rank 0. STRICT_CHALLENGE_RESTRICTED_TAPPING keeps the rewards of a creature tapped by one challenge from characters outside it: in a free-for-all group the partner outside the mode receives neither experience nor the loot of the tapper's kill, while a partner inside the same mode receives both. Each magic difficulty aura reduces healing done by the percentage its tooltip states (tier 1 15%, tier 100 25%); tiers 2 to 100 store it as flat healing done in Spell.dbc, which the server reads as a percentage like tier 1. Each physical difficulty aura periodically triggers Adventurer Mode Random Aggro (888071), which threatens every enemy within 25 yards: at tier 100 every 15 seconds, so a passive creature 12 yards away enters combat with the player. Restricted tapping also keeps the money of a tapped kill inside the challenge: when the tapper loots a kobold's money in a group with a partner outside the mode, the tapper receives all of it and the partner nothing, while two characters outside any challenge in the same group, one of them after leaving the mode, still split a murloc's money evenly.",
